
  <main id="main">

    <section class="page-head">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow">Pricing</span>
        <h1>Clear pricing. <em>No guesswork.</em></h1>
        <p class="lead">Starting prices for every kind of project, an honest list of what changes the cost, and every ongoing cost spelled out before you agree to anything.</p>
        <div class="btn-row page-head__cta">
          <a href="start" class="btn btn--primary" data-track="cta-pricing-estimate">Get an estimate</a>
          <button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost" data-review-open data-track="cta-pricing-tell">Not sure what you need?</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- STARTING PRICES -->
    <section class="section section--tint" id="starting" aria-labelledby="startTitle">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section__head reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">Starting prices</span>
          <h2 id="startTitle">Where projects begin.</h2>
          <p>Entry prices for a fixed, simple scope. Your proposal confirms the exact price before any development.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="price-cols reveal">
          <ul class="price-list">
            <li><a href="services#websites">Websites<small>One page with your services, contact and map</small></a><span class="price"><small>from</small>R1,000</span></li>
            <li><a href="services#dashboards">Dashboards<small>One view of your numbers from one data source</small></a><span class="price"><small>from</small>R2,000</span></li>
            <li><a href="ai-for-business#library">Automations<small>One repetitive task between two tools</small></a><span class="price"><small>from</small>R2,000</span></li>
          </ul>
          <ul class="price-list">
            <li><a href="ai-demos">AI solutions<small>One focused AI tool, e.g. answers from your documents</small></a><span class="price"><small>from</small>R3,500</span></li>
            <li><a href="services#software">Custom software<small>A small tool such as a calculator or tracker</small></a><span class="price"><small>from</small>R4,500</span></li>
            <li><a href="services#google">Google profile setup<small>Set up or fixed, paid when it&rsquo;s done</small></a><span class="price">R450</span></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- WHAT AFFECTS COST / ONGOING -->
    <section class="section" id="cost" aria-labelledby="costTitle">
      <div class="container split">
        <div class="reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">What affects the cost</span>
          <h2 id="costTitle">Scope, not surprises.</h2>
          <ul class="checklist">
            <li><b>Scope:</b> how many pages, screens, steps or users.</li>
            <li><b>Integrations:</b> how many systems it connects to, and whether they have a way in.</li>
            <li><b>Complexity:</b> the rules, exceptions and approvals it has to handle.</li>
            <li><b>Data:</b> whether your information is ready to use or needs cleaning first.</li>
            <li><b>Ongoing requirements:</b> how much support, monitoring and change you need afterwards.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="reveal" id="ongoing">
          <span class="eyebrow">Ongoing costs</span>
          <h2>Listed in your proposal, never added later.</h2>
          <ul class="price-list price-list--compact">
            <li><span class="pl-name">Hosting &amp; domain<small>Keeps a website or tool online · or R500 a year</small></span><span class="price">R50<span class="per">/month</span></span></li>
            <li><span class="pl-name">Care<small>Hosting plus small changes, Google profile and a monthly report</small></span><span class="price">R150<span class="per">/month</span></span></li>
            <li><span class="pl-name">Third-party subscriptions<small>Software you choose to use, billed by the provider</small></span><span class="price">At cost</span></li>
            <li><span class="pl-name">AI usage<small>What the AI provider charges, passed through, never marked up</small></span><span class="price">At cost</span></li>
            <li><span class="pl-name">Support for larger AI systems<small>Monitoring, evaluation and improvements, with an SLA</small></span><span class="price"><small>from</small>R4,500<span class="per">/month</span></span></li>
            <li><span class="pl-name">Future changes<small>Quoted before work starts</small></span><span class="price">R850<span class="per">/hour</span></span></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- PROCESS -->
    <section class="section section--tint" id="process" aria-labelledby="procTitle">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section__head reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">How a project works</span>
          <h2 id="procTitle">You see the price before anything is built.</h2>
        </div>
        <ol class="steps steps--tight reveal">
          <li class="step"><span class="step__num">1</span><h3>Tell us the problem</h3><p>In your own words. No technical terms needed.</p></li>
          <li class="step"><span class="step__num">2</span><h3>We propose a solution</h3><p>We clarify the scope and suggest the simplest thing that works, which isn&rsquo;t always AI.</p></li>
          <li class="step"><span class="step__num">3</span><h3>Fixed proposal &amp; deposit</h3><p>A fixed price before development. Approve it and pay a 40% deposit.</p></li>
          <li class="step"><span class="step__num">4</span><h3>Build &amp; review</h3><p>You review it; agreed changes within the scope are included.</p></li>
          <li class="step"><span class="step__num">5</span><h3>Pay the balance &amp; launch</h3><p>We launch or hand it over as agreed. You own it.</p></li>
        </ol>
        <p class="small muted section__foot reveal">Deposits, revisions, payment, ownership, handover and support are set out in the <a class="inline-link" href="terms">terms</a> before a project starts.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ ROI CALCULATOR ============ -->
    <section class="section" id="roi" aria-labelledby="roiTitle">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section__head section__head--center reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">Is it worth it?</span>
          <h2 id="roiTitle">What is that work costing you?</h2>
          <p>A rough estimate in ten seconds. Discovery replaces it with a measured one.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="roi reveal" data-roi>
          <div class="roi__inputs">
            <label class="roi__field"><span>People doing this work</span><output data-roi-out="people">3</output><input type="range" name="people" min="1" max="50" value="3" /></label>
            <label class="roi__field"><span>Hours each spends on it per week</span><output data-roi-out="hours">5</output><input type="range" name="hours" min="1" max="40" value="5" /></label>
            <label class="roi__field"><span>Their monthly salary (R)</span><output data-roi-out="salary">R25,000</output><input type="range" name="salary" min="8000" max="120000" step="1000" value="25000" /></label>
            <label class="roi__field"><span>Share of that work a system could take over</span><output data-roi-out="share">60%</output><input type="range" name="share" min="20" max="90" step="5" value="60" /></label>
          </div>
          <div class="roi__out" aria-live="polite">
            <div><span>Hours back every month</span><b data-roi="hours">0</b></div>
            <div><span>Value of that time, per month</span><b data-roi="month">R0</b></div>
            <div class="roi__big"><span>Per year</span><b data-roi="year">R0</b></div>
            <p class="tiny muted">Hours × loaded cost (salary × 1.3 ÷ 173 hours). An estimate, not a promise: we measure the real figure in discovery.</p>
            <button type="button" class="btn btn--primary btn--full" data-review-open data-track="cta-roi">Tell us about it</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- IMPLEMENTATION -->
    <section class="section section--tint" id="implementation" aria-labelledby="implTitle">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section__head reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">Larger AI process work</span>
          <h2 id="implTitle">When the job is bigger than a fixed-scope build.</h2>
          <p>Automating a whole process across your software is done in stages you can stop between. Each stage ends with something you keep and a decision, and nothing goes to production before it has proved itself on your work.</p>
        </div>
        <ol class="stages reveal">
          <li><div><span class="stages__k">Start here</span><h3>Process review</h3><p>30 minutes. Where the time goes, whether AI is the answer, and what we&rsquo;d look at first.</p></div><b>Free</b></li>
          <li><div><span class="stages__k">Phases 1–2 · 1–2 weeks</span><h3>Discovery &amp; opportunity map</h3><p>Process map, baseline measurements, every opportunity scored, an ROI estimate and a recommended first build. Yours to keep. Credited in full against implementation if you go ahead within 60 days.</p></div><b>R7,500</b></li>
          <li><div><span class="stages__k">Phases 3–4 · 2–4 weeks</span><h3>Proof of concept</h3><p>The smallest useful version, on real work, measured before vs after. Go, adjust or stop.</p></div><b><small>from</small> R18,500</b></li>
          <li><div><span class="stages__k">Phases 5–6 · fixed quote</span><h3>Production implementation</h3><p>Integrated with your software, with permissions, logging and safe fallbacks, documented, and your team trained.</p></div><b><small>from</small> R45,000</b></li>
        </ol>
        <p class="small muted section__foot reveal">A 40% deposit starts each paid stage and comes off its price; the balance is due on completion. Larger implementations can be split across milestones. <a class="inline-link" href="terms">Terms</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- OPERATIONS -->
    <section class="section" id="operations" aria-labelledby="opsTitle">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section__head section__head--center reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">Operations</span>
          <h2 id="opsTitle">Run, measured and improved, every month.</h2>
          <p>Starts at go-live, with a 3-month minimum and then month to month. Every plan includes monitoring, model and API costs up to its allowance, maintenance, security updates, usage monitoring, evaluation, support to the SLA, improvement hours, and a monthly ROI report.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid plans plans--3">
          <div class="card plan reveal">
            <h3>Operate</h3>
            <div class="plan__price">R4,500<small>/month</small></div>
            <p>One system, kept running and reported on.</p>
            <ul><li>1 system covered</li><li>Model &amp; API costs up to R750 a month</li><li>1 hour a month for optimisation</li><li>Accuracy evaluation every quarter</li><li>Monthly ROI report</li><li>Support: next business day</li></ul>
          </div>
          <div class="card plan plan--featured reveal">
            <span class="plan__flag">Most chosen</span>
            <h3>Optimise</h3>
            <div class="plan__price">R9,500<small>/month</small></div>
            <p>For systems that should keep getting better.</p>
            <ul><li>Up to 3 systems</li><li>Model &amp; API costs up to R2,500 a month</li><li>4 hours a month for workflow improvements and small integrations</li><li>Accuracy evaluation every month</li><li>Monthly ROI report, quarterly roadmap review</li><li>Support: within 4 business hours</li></ul>
          </div>
          <div class="card plan reveal">
            <h3>Partner</h3>
            <div class="plan__price">R18,500<small>/month</small></div>
            <p>AI operations as a standing capability.</p>
            <ul><li>All systems in the agreement</li><li>Model &amp; API costs up to R6,000 a month</li><li>10 hours a month, unused hours roll over one month</li><li>Accuracy evaluation every month</li><li>Monthly ROI report and review call, monthly roadmap</li><li>Support: within 2 business hours; critical within 1</li></ul>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="center small muted section__foot reveal">Model and API use above the allowance is billed at cost, and we warn you at 80%. Unused hours don&rsquo;t roll over, except on Partner (one month).</p>

        <div class="table-wrap reveal" id="sla" style="margin-top:2rem">
          <table class="spec spec--sla">
            <caption>Service levels</caption>
            <thead><tr><th scope="col"></th><th scope="col">Operate</th><th scope="col">Optimise</th><th scope="col">Partner</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><th scope="row">Critical: down, or wrong outputs at scale</th><td>Next business day</td><td>4 business hours</td><td>1 business hour</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">High: a part failing, with a workaround</th><td>Next business day</td><td>4 business hours</td><td>2 business hours</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Normal: questions and requests</th><td>2 business days</td><td>Next business day</td><td>4 business hours</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Monitoring &amp; alerts</th><td>✓</td><td>✓</td><td>✓</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Security updates &amp; maintenance</th><td>✓</td><td>✓</td><td>✓</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Accuracy evaluation</th><td>Quarterly</td><td>Monthly</td><td>Monthly</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="small muted reveal" style="margin-top:0.8rem">Business hours are Monday to Friday, 08:00–17:00 SAST, excluding public holidays. Response time is a person acknowledging the issue with a first assessment, not a guaranteed fix time. We monitor the AI providers we use but can&rsquo;t guarantee their uptime; we guarantee how fast we respond and that your system falls back safely.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- SEPARATE -->
    <section class="section section--tint" id="separate" aria-labelledby="sepTitle">
      <div class="container split">
        <div class="reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">Priced separately</span>
          <h2 id="sepTitle">Outside the scope? It has a price before it starts.</h2>
          <p class="lead">This is what keeps implementation fixed and operations predictable. Small changes come out of your plan&rsquo;s hours first.</p>
        </div>
        <ul class="price-list reveal">
          <li><span class="pl-name">Change requests<small>Beyond your plan&rsquo;s hours, quoted before work starts</small></span><span class="price">R850<span class="per">/hour</span></span></li>
          <li><span class="pl-name">New functionality<small>A new capability is its own project, with its own fixed quote</small></span><span class="price">Quoted</span></li>
          <li><span class="pl-name">Consulting &amp; workshops<small>Half-day workshop R4,500</small></span><span class="price">R1,250<span class="per">/hour</span></span></li>
          <li><span class="pl-name">Emergency support<small>Outside SLA hours, 1-hour minimum</small></span><span class="price">R1,650<span class="per">/hour</span></span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- WORKED EXAMPLE -->
    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="fyTitle">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section__head section__head--center reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">A worked example</span>
          <h2 id="fyTitle">What it costs, and when it pays back.</h2>
          <p>Example numbers for enquiry handling at a 15-person firm. Yours come from your own baseline in discovery.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ex reveal">
          <table class="spec">
            <caption>Cost</caption>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>Discovery</td><td class="price">R7,500</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Proof of concept</td><td class="price">R18,500</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Production implementation</td><td class="price">R45,000</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Less discovery credit</td><td class="price">−R7,500</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>Implementation, total</strong></td><td class="price"><strong>R63,500</strong></td></tr>
              <tr><td>Operations (Operate)</td><td class="price">R4,500/mo</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
          <table class="spec">
            <caption>Value</caption>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>4 people × 10 hours a week on enquiries</td><td class="price">173 h/mo</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Share the system takes over (measured)</td><td class="price">60%</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Hours back</td><td class="price">104 h/mo</td></tr>
              <tr><td>At R28,000 salary (loaded ≈ R210/h)</td><td class="price">R21,870/mo</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Less operations</td><td class="price">−R4,500/mo</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>Payback</strong></td><td class="price"><strong>≈ 3.7 months</strong></td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="center small muted section__foot reveal">Hours × loaded cost (salary × 1.3 ÷ 173). Revenue effects such as faster replies winning more work are reported separately, and only when measured. <a class="inline-link" href="method#measure">How we measure</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- WEBSITES -->
    <section class="section section--tint" id="websites" aria-labelledby="pricesTitle">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="price-head reveal">
          <div>
            <span class="eyebrow">Websites</span>
            <h2 id="pricesTitle">Websites, hosting and Google.</h2>
            <p class="muted">Still part of what we do, for small businesses that need to be found. A fixed quote first; a 40% deposit when you accept.</p>
          </div>
          <p class="callout"><strong>Rather not pay upfront?</strong> A one-page website with Care is <strong>R249 a month for 12 months</strong>, then R150 a month for Care. It costs a little more than paying upfront (R2,988 over the year, against R2,500).</p>
        </div>
        <div class="price-cols reveal">
          <div class="price-group">
            <h3>Builds</h3>
            <ul class="price-list price-list--compact">
              <li><a href="services#websites">Quick website<small>1 page, live in about a day</small></a><span class="price"><small>from</small>R1,000</span></li>
              <li><a href="services#websites">Business website<small>Up to 4–5 pages, custom layout</small></a><span class="price"><small>from</small>R2,000</span></li>
              <li><a href="services#websites">Custom website<small>Booking, online shop, portals</small></a><span class="price"><small>from</small>R4,500</span></li>
              <li><a href="services#websites">Changes to a site<small>Text, hours, images, small content</small></a><span class="price"><small>from</small>R250</span></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="price-group" id="care">
            <h3>Hosting &amp; Care</h3>
            <ul class="price-list price-list--compact">
              <li><span class="pl-name">Hosting<small>Online, secure, backed up, monitored · or R500 a year</small></span><span class="price">R50<span class="per">/month</span></span></li>
              <li><span class="pl-name">Care<small>Hosting, small changes, Google profile kept current, monthly report · or R1,500 a year</small></span><span class="price">R150<span class="per">/month</span></span></li>
              <li><a href="services#google">Google profile setup<small>Comes off a website built within 90 days</small></a><span class="price">R450</span></li>
            </ul>
            <p class="tiny muted" style="margin:0.6rem 0 0">A new website&rsquo;s quote includes its first year of Care. Keep a small &ldquo;Website by Re-Charge&rdquo; link and your plan is R100 a year cheaper; refer a business that goes live and your next year of Care is free.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="btn-row reveal" style="margin-top:1.2rem">
          <a href="start" class="btn btn--ghost">Get a website estimate</a>
          <button type="button" class="btn btn--free" data-mockup-open>Free mockup <span class="btn__tag">Free</span></button>
        </div>
        <div class="offer-note" data-offer-note hidden></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- HOW WE WORK -->
    <section class="section" id="how-we-work" aria-labelledby="rulesTitle">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section__head reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">The rules</span>
          <h2 id="rulesTitle">What keeps every engagement fair.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="rules reveal">
          <div class="rule"><h3>Defined scope</h3><p>Every project has a written scope and a fixed price before development. If the scope holds, the price holds.</p></div>
          <div class="rule"><h3>Ongoing costs up front</h3><p>Hosting, subscriptions, AI usage and support are listed in your proposal, never added later.</p></div>
          <div class="rule"><h3>Changes are priced</h3><p>Change requests, new functionality, consulting and emergencies each have their own rate, agreed before work starts.</p></div>
          <div class="rule"><h3>You own it</h3><p>Your data, accounts, code and documentation are yours. Leave any time after the minimum and take it all with you.</p></div>
        </div>
        <p class="small muted section__foot reveal">Already with us on AI Care or the Partner retainer? You keep your current plan and price until you choose to change. Full terms are on the <a class="inline-link" href="terms">Terms</a> page.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- FAQ -->
    <section class="section section--tint" id="faq" aria-labelledby="pricingFaqTitle">
      <div class="container container--narrow">
        <div class="section__head section__head--center reveal">
          <span class="eyebrow">Pricing questions</span>
          <h2 id="pricingFaqTitle">Common questions about cost.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="faq reveal">
          <details class="faq__item"><summary>What do I get at the starting price?</summary><p>The simplest useful version: a one-page website, one dashboard from one data source, one automation between two tools, one focused AI tool, or a small custom tool. More pages, sources, integrations or users add to the price, and your proposal shows exactly what&rsquo;s included.</p></details>
          <details class="faq__item"><summary>Why doesn&rsquo;t every project cost the starting price?</summary><p>Because a one-page site and a booking system with payments are both &ldquo;websites&rdquo;, but they&rsquo;re not the same work. Starting prices tell you where a project begins; the fixed proposal tells you what yours costs, before anything is built.</p></details>
          <details class="faq__item"><summary>Why isn&rsquo;t discovery free?</summary><p>Because it&rsquo;s the most valuable part: a map of your processes, measured baselines and a scored list of opportunities. You keep it whether or not you build with us, and it&rsquo;s credited in full if you do within 60 days. The process review before it is free.</p></details>
          <details class="faq__item"><summary>Can we stop after the proof of concept?</summary><p>Yes. That&rsquo;s what it&rsquo;s for. If the measured result doesn&rsquo;t justify production, we&rsquo;ll say so, and you&rsquo;ve only paid for the proof of concept.</p></details>
          <details class="faq__item"><summary>Why is Operations a monthly fee?</summary><p>AI systems aren&rsquo;t finished at go-live. Models change, your processes change, and accuracy drifts if nobody checks it. Operations covers the model and API costs, monitoring, security, evaluation, support and improvements, and proves the value every month.</p></details>
          <details class="faq__item"><summary>What if our AI usage goes above the allowance?</summary><p>We warn you at 80% of the allowance. Anything above it is billed at cost, never marked up. If it keeps happening, we&rsquo;ll suggest the plan or design change that brings it down.</p></details>
          <details class="faq__item"><summary>Do you still build websites?</summary><p>Yes, from R1,000 with a free preview first, plus Hosting and Care plans. They&rsquo;re priced and run separately from the AI work.</p></details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="cta" aria-labelledby="pricingCtaTitle">
      <div class="container cta__inner reveal">
        <h2 id="pricingCtaTitle">Have a question before committing?</h2>
        <p>Ask it. Tell us what you&rsquo;re trying to improve and we&rsquo;ll tell you honestly what it would cost, including the ongoing part.</p>
        <div class="btn-row btn-row--center">
          <button type="button" class="btn btn--light btn--large" data-review-open data-track="cta-pricing-final">Tell us what&rsquo;s slowing you down</button>
          <a href="start" class="btn btn--ghost-light btn--large">Get an estimate</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>

